<title>BELGIUM: Belgian April yr-yr budget surplus widens. [CORRECTED 12:48 GMT]</title>
<headline>Belgian April yr-yr budget surplus widens. [CORRECTED 12:48 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian federal state's net budget surplus (Corrects from borrowing requirement) widened to 39.4 billion francs in April 1997 from 17.5 billion in the year-ago month, the Finance and Budget Ministries said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>The cumulative borrowing requirement for the first four months of 1997 widened to 203.7 billion francs from 199.6 billion in the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
